cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "qsafe-certs: quantum-safe, long-term verification of academic certificates"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype that keeps digital degree certificates verifiable for decades
  as signature algorithms are broken. Certificates carry post-quantum signatures
  (ML-DSA, SLH-DSA); a renewable evidence chain, after RFC 4998, proves when each
  certificate existed; and every timestamp must be signed by at least k of n
  independent timestamp authorities. Includes tests, benchmarks, a k-of-n
  security and availability study, and a Streamlit demo.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yamini Punyavathi
    family-names: Muttevi
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yamini-Muttevi/qsafe-certs"
license: MIT
version: "0.1"
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - ML-DSA
  - SLH-DSA
  - evidence records
  - timestamping
  - long-term archiving
  - academic credentials
